name w4-06-decoy
timeout 500
time 1999-04-14T10:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W4, SORTIE 6 OF 10 - ALLIED FORCE 1999. THE DECOYS.
# CONTROL: w4-04-emitter-hunt.fbm - identical but for ONE fact, three more emitters, and the callsign
# prefix. Spec: doc/campaigns/w4-allied-force.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# THE ANCHOR names decoys as a decisive Yugoslav measure - "extensive use of decoys" [T3] - and W4's
# own cast table asks for "a radar decoy: ground, emitting, not lethal", which it books as `C1` and
# which `doc/modules/ground/cast.md` costs at "the `p18` row with `rounds 0` and a small range gate".
# RE-CHECKED AGAINST THE TREE (rule 7), AND THE ANSWER IS SHARPER THAN THE ENTRY: a `p18` HAS no
# weapon at all (`Channels 0`, `RoundsDefault 0`), so the decoy needs no `rounds 0` and no new row -
# it is the SAME ROW as the net's own early-warning node, at the same 250 km range gate, radiating the
# same `SurfaceEarlyWarning` beam. The half of the entry that CANNOT be built is "a small range gate":
# there is no `set` key for a position's search range, and inventing one would be a catalogue change.
# SO IN THIS TREE A DECOY IS NOT A WEAKER EMITTER, IT IS AN IDENTICAL ONE IN A DIFFERENT PLACE - and
# that is exactly the situation the anchor describes and exactly what makes the question worth asking.
#
# THE THREE DECOYS are `k6dka` 42.78000 20.93000, `k6dkb` 42.80000 20.93500, `k6dkc` 42.76000 20.93500
# - all [SET], all WEST of the real node (42.78000 20.95000), i.e. between the shooters and it, which
# is where a decoy belt belongs. THEIR RANGE IS NOT FREE, AND THE FLOOR SETS IT: a P-18's elevation
# coverage tops out at +15 deg, so from 4,572 m nothing closer than 4,572/tan(15) = 17.06 km is
# audible at all. A first cut of this file put the belt at 13.5 km and it was INAUDIBLE - three
# decoys that changed not one byte of the run. The belt is therefore at 18.4-18.9 km, just inside the
# node's 20.0 km, and that is the depth the floor leaves a decoy belt: about 3 km. They are on NO net: a decoy that could cue a battery would be a
# battery. That is also the one honest discriminator `air-defence-network.md` names - "a decoy is
# never on the net, so it never comes up on a cue" - and no sensor in this tree can read it.
#
# THE FOUR STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES: see w4-01-floor.fbm.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: CAN A RADIATING POSITION WITH NO WEAPON TAKE THE ROUND MEANT FOR THE ONE
# THAT HAS ONE?
#
# READING RULE (binding): exit 3 = TIMEOUT. Read `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE ... signal=`, then
# `missile SEEKER_ACTIVE ... symbol= kind= signal=`, then WHERE each round came down
# (`stores IMPACT crossLat/crossLon`) against the four positions' coordinates, then `UNIT_RESULT` for
# `k6nod` and the three decoys. The RWR measures received power and never range - that is the whole
# mechanism, and it is `sensors.md`'s own contract, not a decoy model.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint 77232651160faceb, exit 3): YES, COMPLETELY - AND THE DECOY IS THE SAME ROW AS
# THE THING IT PROTECTS.
#   the pilot's cue    `ATTACK_RELEASE ... kind=surface-search signal=0.998623` at t=0.1 against 04's
#                      0.998373. Received power is `1 - (r/2R)^2` and the whole belt is `p18` at the
#                      same 250 km gate, so the LOUDEST admissible symbol is simply the NEAREST one -
#                      a decoy 1.6 km closer than the node. The pilot cannot tell and by contract must
#                      not be able to: the receiver measures power and never range
#   the rounds         BOTH AGM-88 latch a decoy and BOTH kill it: `stores DETONATION ... target=k6dka
#                      missM=0.0192` at t=58.6 and `missM=4.753` at t=59.7. `k6dka` DESTROYED by 2 hits
#   what it cost the defence   NOTHING. `k6nod` INTACT, `k6sam` INTACT, `k6sa3` INTACT
#   what it cost the attacker  the node AND the suppression: `mission SUPPRESSION_LOST ... k6nod
#                      emittingS=120.1 allowanceS=120` at t=120.1, where 04 read SUPPRESSED at 66.5
#   AND THE SECOND-ORDER PRICE IS THE ONE WORTH READING: with the node alive the whole run, the net
#   goes on cueing - `net CUE` **26 against 04's 4** - and the 2K12, which fires NOTHING in 04 because
#   the node dies inside its 26 s reaction, here fires **all three 3M9** (t=110.0 / 136.9 / 163.8). The
#   belt's total expenditure goes 4 -> **7 launches**. TWO TIN SHEDS' WORTH OF EMISSION BOUGHT THE
#   DEFENCE ITS NODE, ITS CUE TRAFFIC AND THREE MORE ROUNDS IN THE AIR.
#   THE STRIKE IS UNCHANGED: 2 of 2 strikers release at the identical ticks, `aimErrM` 48.07 / 54.15 m.
#   THE HONEST LIMIT, STATED: this works because a decoy and an early-warning node are the SAME
#   catalogue row. The `arm_class` filter is the only sort that exists, and it is binary - `any` and
#   `early_warning` see the whole belt including the decoys, `fire_control` sees NONE of them (a `p18`
#   and a SAM's search set are both `SurfaceEarlyWarning`, and a fire-control beam exists only while a
#   position is tracking). So today the choice is: hunt early-warning sets and be decoyed, or hunt
#   fire-control sets and hear nothing until a battery is already shooting at you.
#   AND THE FLOOR SETS THE BELT'S DEPTH, which is a second measured consequence of sortie 04's number:
#   nothing inside 3,000/tan(15) = 11.2 km is audible to a Weasel at 3,000 m, so a decoy belt has to
#   stand off. A first cut of this file put it at 13.5 km with the shooters at 4,572 m, where the limit
#   is 17.1 km, and the three decoys changed NOT ONE BYTE of the run.

net kosnet6
  control k6nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member k6nod
  member k6sam autonomy hold
  member k6sa3 autonomy hold

unit k6wsa
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ws4 1
  spawn 42.78000 20.70560 3000 90.0 480     # 20.0 km west of the node, AT the floor
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 agm88
  set store 7 agm88
  set arm_class any
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode arm
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.78000 20.90000 3000 480
  wp 42.78000 20.50000 3000 480
  objective suppress unit k6nod emitting 120
  objective survive

unit k6wsb
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ws4 2
  spawn 42.75000 20.70560 3150 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 agm88
  set store 7 agm88
  set arm_class any
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode arm
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.75000 20.90000 3150 480
  wp 42.75000 20.50000 3150 480
  objective survive

unit k6stra
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight st4 1
  spawn 42.70000 20.55000 4572 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.70000 21.15000 4572 450
  wp 42.70000 20.60000 4572 450
  objective kill unit k6tgt
  objective survive

unit k6strb
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight st4 2
  spawn 42.67000 20.55000 4720 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.67000 21.18000 4720 450
  wp 42.67000 20.60000 4720 450
  objective kill unit k6hgr
  objective survive

unit k6nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 42.78000 20.95000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free

unit k6sam
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.10000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon hold
  set rounds 3

unit k6sa3
  module sa3
  team hostile
  spawn 42.62000 21.05000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon hold
  set rounds 4

unit k6tgt
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.15000 ground 90.0 0

unit k6hgr
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 42.67000 21.18000 ground 90.0 0

unit k6dka
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 42.78000 20.93000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free

unit k6dkb
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 42.80000 20.93500 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free

unit k6dkc
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 42.76000 20.93500 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free
